WEBVTT

00:02.880 --> 00:05.090
A long, long time ago.

00:05.300 --> 00:08.170
A story from about a hundred years ago.

00:08.970 --> 00:13.430
Nadja, guided by destiny, arrived in Italy

00:17.470 --> 00:18.770
NAAJA

00:17.470 --> 00:18.770
Nadja,

00:18.890 --> 00:21.440
With your eyes

00:18.890 --> 00:21.440
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:21.440 --> 00:22.650
Nadja,

00:21.440 --> 00:22.650
NAAJA

00:22.690 --> 00:24.940
What do you see?

00:22.690 --> 00:24.940
Nani ga mieru

00:24.980 --> 00:27.860
Shining in the far distance,

00:24.980 --> 00:27.860
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:27.860 --> 00:30.240
The door to the future,

00:27.860 --> 00:30.240
Mirai no tobira

00:31.160 --> 00:34.620
That's what I'm searching for

00:31.160 --> 00:34.620
Sagashite iru

00:34.620 --> 00:41.830
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:42.540 --> 00:46.040
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:42.540 --> 00:46.040
Minna egao de aetara

00:46.130 --> 00:49.380
I'm sure there would be no more fighting

00:46.130 --> 00:49.380
Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:49.420 --> 00:52.630
It could be so much more fun

00:49.420 --> 00:52.630
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:52.680 --> 00:56.100
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:52.680 --> 00:56.100
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:56.470 --> 00:59.770
I can't see the end of the journey

00:56.470 --> 00:59.770
Tabi no owari wa mienai

00:59.890 --> 01:03.230
God is the only one who could possibly know

00:59.890 --> 01:03.230
Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:03.400 --> 01:06.980
To the people who, someday, I will meet again

01:03.400 --> 01:06.980
Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:07.020 --> 01:09.150
I will go waving

01:07.020 --> 01:09.150
Te wo furinagara

01:09.230 --> 01:15.910
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:09.230 --> 01:15.910
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:15.950 --> 01:18.660
But I won't look back

01:15.950 --> 01:18.660
Ushiro mukanai

01:18.990 --> 01:23.960
Until the day my dream comes true

01:18.990 --> 01:23.960
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:24.250 --> 01:27.670
Nadja, Your smile

01:24.250 --> 01:27.670
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:27.750 --> 01:31.090
Nadja, gives me courage

01:27.750 --> 01:31.090
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:31.130 --> 01:34.050
Under the blue sky,

01:31.130 --> 01:34.050
Aoi sora no shita de

01:34.180 --> 01:37.010
I will find the place

01:34.180 --> 01:37.010
Ashita no yukue

01:37.300 --> 01:41.230
where my future lies

01:37.300 --> 01:41.230
Mitsukeru kara

01:47.630 --> 01:49.670
﻿The pride of our Dandelion Troupe...

01:49.670 --> 01:51.250
﻿...the miraculous dancing princess, Nadja...

01:51.460 --> 01:52.420
﻿...and the samurai, Kennosuke's...

01:52.840 --> 01:55.220
﻿Italian Flag show!

02:50.570 --> 02:52.770
﻿Eh? Granny's birthday?

02:53.190 --> 02:54.070
﻿That's correct.

02:54.360 --> 02:57.280
Uh... if I recall, she'll be 80 years old today.

02:57.820 --> 02:59.860
﻿Isn't she still 60 years old?

03:02.330 --> 03:04.040
﻿What? 90 years old?

03:05.910 --> 03:08.250
﻿I heard she was 99...

03:08.460 --> 03:12.880
﻿But, Abel says she's 257 years old and probably a witch.

03:12.880 --> 03:14.590
﻿Ugh... a witch...

03:14.880 --> 03:16.420
﻿How old is she, really?

03:16.420 --> 03:17.260
﻿Who knows?

03:18.430 --> 03:21.050
﻿Anyway, today is Granny's birthday...

03:21.550 --> 03:24.640
﻿We'll have a party tonight, so prepare some birthday presents...

03:25.390 --> 03:26.850
﻿Huh? Now?

03:27.180 --> 03:29.770
﻿After the performance, how about we go look for something?

03:33.900 --> 03:36.110
﻿Wow! What an expensive-looking carriage!

03:36.240 --> 03:38.400
﻿I wonder what kind of person is riding in it.

03:41.660 --> 03:44.240
﻿Huh? A performance by traveling performers...

03:45.120 --> 03:46.540
﻿It looks fun.

03:46.660 --> 03:48.250
﻿I would love to see it.

03:48.710 --> 03:50.330
﻿The tricks of traveling performers...

03:50.330 --> 03:52.540
﻿...are not worth going to see.

03:53.630 --> 03:54.880
﻿Oh father...

04:03.780 --> 04:08.790
Mother and Daughter Who Keep Passing Each Other
The Two Birthdays

04:10.560 --> 04:12.060
﻿Duke Preminger..

04:12.360 --> 04:14.060
﻿Count and Countess Waltmüller...

04:14.400 --> 04:15.730
﻿We have been awaiting your arrival.

04:17.230 --> 04:18.360
﻿Thank you for your kind regards.

04:23.740 --> 04:24.820
﻿Oscar...?

04:31.790 --> 04:33.290
﻿It has been a while since we last met.

04:34.460 --> 04:35.750
﻿You surprised me.

04:36.300 --> 04:38.090
﻿I thought you were in Vienna.

04:38.300 --> 04:41.800
﻿I could not stand the atmosphere at home, so I came to take a break.

04:42.260 --> 04:44.090
﻿You must have had a fight with Herman again.

04:44.390 --> 04:45.390
﻿Yes, well...

04:48.770 --> 04:50.230
﻿Oh! Excuse me.

04:50.480 --> 04:53.400
﻿I have an appointment, so I have to leave before you.

04:53.600 --> 04:54.190
﻿Yes.
All right.

04:54.860 --> 04:58.230
﻿Until I come back, please keep Colette company.

05:02.570 --> 05:03.820
﻿Go on, dear.

05:04.220 --> 05:04.680
Yes.

05:05.870 --> 05:07.780
﻿What a big difference from my parents...

05:09.290 --> 05:11.250
﻿As you know, Aunt Colette...

05:12.040 --> 05:13.580
﻿My father acts like a dictator...

05:14.420 --> 05:16.710
﻿Why did my mother remarry herself to the likes of him?

05:17.590 --> 05:19.340
﻿Oscar, I'm sorry.

05:19.340 --> 05:20.550
﻿Ah! Don't be.

05:21.130 --> 05:24.630
﻿However, for a person like my father, to be your younger brother...

05:25.090 --> 05:27.050
﻿I still find it hard to believe.

05:27.810 --> 05:28.810
﻿On this occasion as well...

05:29.180 --> 05:31.770
﻿...regarding the ball which was to be my debut into society...

05:35.690 --> 05:36.810
﻿Hey, Oscar!

05:37.360 --> 05:39.520
﻿Put on your best clothes for this!

05:39.730 --> 05:44.200
﻿You have to catch a woman with a big dowry!

05:49.030 --> 05:50.330
﻿To think he said something like that...

05:51.540 --> 05:54.040
﻿I feel nauseated by that kind of thinking.

05:54.870 --> 05:57.960
﻿I don't even want to go to the ball anymore.

05:58.420 --> 05:59.380
﻿Oscar...

06:00.920 --> 06:03.050
﻿You should go to that ball.

06:03.550 --> 06:04.090
﻿But...

06:04.590 --> 06:08.760
﻿You might meet someone special there...

06:09.260 --> 06:10.760
﻿Like I did.

06:14.060 --> 06:15.560
﻿What nice weather..

06:16.020 --> 06:17.770
﻿Will you walk with me?

06:23.570 --> 06:26.070
﻿I met my first husband, Raymond...

06:26.320 --> 06:28.870
﻿...at my first ball.

06:36.750 --> 06:38.500
﻿To my 16 years old self...

06:38.790 --> 06:42.210
﻿...the ball seemed like a glittering, different world from my own.

06:53.100 --> 06:54.770
﻿I danced with so many people...

06:55.100 --> 06:56.940
﻿And, everything was so new..

06:57.940 --> 07:01.440
﻿Eventually, I started to feel closed in.

07:24.670 --> 07:25.760
﻿Who is it?

08:01.290 --> 08:03.130
﻿Um, I'm sorry...

08:03.630 --> 08:05.710
﻿I heard the sound of a lovely piano...

08:11.140 --> 08:13.390
﻿You're like... a fairy...

08:17.020 --> 08:19.680
﻿Ah! Uh... no... I...

08:19.690 --> 08:21.350
I ﻿came to Vienna to study...

08:21.350 --> 08:23.400
﻿I'm a Frenchman.

08:23.730 --> 08:27.280
﻿Um, tonight, a friend invited me here...

08:27.940 --> 08:30.700
﻿But, balls don't seem to be my style...

08:31.320 --> 08:32.160
﻿My...!

08:39.710 --> 08:40.710
﻿A waltz?

08:44.460 --> 08:45.080
﻿Um...

08:46.340 --> 08:47.300
﻿It's not my style, but...

08:48.670 --> 08:51.220
﻿Would you be so kind as to dance with me?

08:54.600 --> 08:55.220
﻿Yes...

09:14.200 --> 09:15.570
﻿I wanted to see him again...

09:15.740 --> 09:18.240
﻿And, afterwards I looked for him at other balls...

09:18.700 --> 09:20.540
﻿But, he never appeared...

09:21.250 --> 09:23.210
﻿Even then, I wouldn't forget him...

09:23.420 --> 09:27.540
﻿And, I had a music box that played the waltz we danced to... specially made.

09:31.720 --> 09:33.050
﻿Day after day...

09:33.050 --> 09:37.050
﻿I listened to the music box and thought about him.

09:39.600 --> 09:41.560
﻿Hey! Nadja! Let's go!

09:41.770 --> 09:42.390
﻿Oh!

09:43.390 --> 09:45.140
﻿Okay! I'm coming.

09:51.940 --> 09:53.650
﻿What should we get as a present?

09:53.900 --> 09:55.200
﻿Well..

09:55.410 --> 09:58.490
﻿What would Granny like?

10:02.960 --> 10:05.080
﻿Two years from that ball...

10:05.670 --> 10:08.840
﻿A new piano teacher was supposed to come to the house...

10:17.300 --> 10:18.970
﻿As if the goddess of destiny...

10:18.970 --> 10:20.600
﻿...was pushing our backs..

10:20.970 --> 10:23.430
﻿...we were drawn together...

10:33.440 --> 10:36.110
﻿But, that man, Raymond...

10:36.410 --> 10:38.110
﻿...was not of the aristocracy, was he?

10:38.530 --> 10:39.320
﻿Yes...

10:39.830 --> 10:43.540
﻿Father was not the kind of person to allow a love beyond social bounds...

10:47.370 --> 10:49.290
﻿He's fired!

10:49.420 --> 10:51.420
﻿I'll make sure he will never be able to stay in Vienna as well!

10:52.800 --> 10:54.170
﻿Father!

11:04.640 --> 11:07.690
﻿I left the house in Vienna without saying anything to Father...

11:07.940 --> 11:11.610
﻿And, decided to make a new life with Raymond.

11:41.260 --> 11:45.720
﻿My life in Paris with Raymond was poor but happy...

12:16.090 --> 12:18.260
﻿And, our child was born...

12:22.850 --> 12:23.510
﻿Nadja...

12:24.300 --> 12:27.060
﻿My dearest child with Raymond...

12:33.810 --> 12:36.980
﻿Nadja loved music from the time she was born...

12:37.280 --> 12:41.990
﻿When he played the piano, she used to move her body as if she was dancing...

12:45.780 --> 12:47.870
﻿Her favorite song of all was...

12:48.040 --> 12:50.710
...a ﻿lullaby that Raymond wrote.

12:57.840 --> 13:00.590
﻿I wonder what Granny would like...

13:02.590 --> 13:05.340
﻿The age difference between us is so great, I can't even guess.

13:06.760 --> 13:08.430
﻿My dead mother...

13:08.430 --> 13:11.930
﻿...liked it when I massaged her shoulders.

13:13.980 --> 13:16.520
﻿I wonder what my mother likes?

13:18.440 --> 13:22.570
﻿I'm always imagining different things about my mother...

13:23.030 --> 13:26.200
﻿Like, I wonder what mother's doing now?

13:26.450 --> 13:30.040
﻿Or, what kind of dances did she dance in that dress?

13:30.870 --> 13:32.460
It'﻿s a lot of fun!

13:34.960 --> 13:35.670
﻿I know!

13:36.210 --> 13:38.840
﻿Let's try imagining about Granny!

13:40.510 --> 13:43.130
﻿I'm sure when Granny was young, she wore a dress...

13:43.260 --> 13:44.720
﻿...and danced a lot, too.

13:50.310 --> 13:52.270
﻿Maybe, she was a great beauty in the old days...

13:52.680 --> 13:55.480
﻿Maybe, she had a passionate romance with a lovely man...

13:56.190 --> 13:57.860
﻿G-Granny, a romance?

13:58.110 --> 13:59.270
﻿No way!

13:59.860 --> 14:01.280
﻿What do you mean by "no way"?

14:01.490 --> 14:04.360
﻿Granny didn't start out old, you know!

14:05.320 --> 14:07.990
﻿Wow, that's so pretty! Thank you!

14:07.990 --> 14:08.660
﻿Huh?

14:08.950 --> 14:10.080
﻿I love you.

14:12.700 --> 14:13.330
﻿Shall we go?

14:13.330 --> 14:13.830
﻿Yes.

14:13.960 --> 14:15.290
﻿That's it! I have it!

14:17.330 --> 14:18.420
﻿Hey, Nadja!

14:18.960 --> 14:19.500
﻿Excuse me...

14:19.800 --> 14:21.500
Yes, ﻿may I help you?

14:21.800 --> 14:24.170
﻿Will you let us help you sell these?

14:24.550 --> 14:25.090
﻿Huh?

14:28.010 --> 14:29.680
﻿Would you like some flowers?

14:29.680 --> 14:31.100
﻿Beautiful flowers!

14:32.700 --> 14:36.040
Hello, hello, how are you?

14:36.250 --> 14:39.500
The people of England!

14:39.670 --> 14:43.170
Bonjour, Bonjour, how are you?

14:43.170 --> 14:46.470
The people of France!

15:04.130 --> 15:08.880
﻿But, our happy life in France didn't last long...

15:10.760 --> 15:12.050
In an accident, Raymond...

15:17.980 --> 15:20.770
﻿But, just because Raymond died...

15:20.940 --> 15:23.190
﻿I couldn't just sit there and cry...

15:25.280 --> 15:28.400
To ﻿raise my daughter, I went to work...

15:29.070 --> 15:30.910
﻿But, it was hard..

15:31.160 --> 15:33.580
﻿And, we both ended up sick...

15:35.160 --> 15:38.080
﻿For many days, we burned with fevers...

15:39.420 --> 15:41.830
﻿I became desperate...

15:42.420 --> 15:45.590
﻿God, I will willingly come to you...

15:45.590 --> 15:48.130
﻿So, please spare my daughter's life...!

15:50.550 --> 15:53.550
﻿But, when my fever broke and I regained consciousness...

15:54.810 --> 15:59.140
﻿...in front of me were my nanny, Edna, and the butler...

16:02.440 --> 16:04.320
﻿The baby didn't survive...

16:13.280 --> 16:14.160
﻿Even now...

16:14.740 --> 16:17.200
﻿I still feel that pain, right here...

16:17.750 --> 16:19.120
﻿...when I think of it.

16:19.620 --> 16:20.620
﻿Aunt...

16:24.130 --> 16:28.420
﻿Edna and the butler were ordered by my father, who had found out where I was...

16:28.590 --> 16:30.760
﻿...to take me back.

16:32.470 --> 16:35.350
﻿For several years after I returned to the house in Vienna...

16:35.350 --> 16:37.560
﻿I spent my days crying...

16:38.600 --> 16:41.140
﻿But, my childhood friend, Albert...

16:41.850 --> 16:45.900
﻿I will cherish all of you, including your past...

16:48.990 --> 16:51.990
﻿And so, I married him.

16:52.240 --> 16:53.360
﻿I understand now...

16:55.580 --> 16:59.040
﻿Some say it's no use counting the birthdays of a dead child...

16:59.500 --> 17:02.580
﻿But, she's still here in my heart...

17:04.840 --> 17:08.750
﻿Every year on her birthday, I buy another one...

17:09.260 --> 17:14.300
﻿With the hope that she and Raymond are happy in heaven...

17:15.010 --> 17:16.140
﻿I see...

17:16.430 --> 17:19.430
﻿If she was alive, she would be 12 years old.

17:20.390 --> 17:22.350
﻿No...

17:22.600 --> 17:23.520
﻿I'm home!

17:24.520 --> 17:27.480
﻿Welcome back.

17:28.480 --> 17:29.730
﻿I picked it up.

17:33.160 --> 17:34.660
﻿Thank you, darling.

17:41.000 --> 17:42.160
﻿Ah! Then...

17:42.660 --> 17:44.710
﻿Today is her birthday...

17:45.040 --> 17:47.250
﻿My child in heaven is 13 years old.

17:51.340 --> 17:54.260
﻿Happy birthday, Nadja.

17:56.890 --> 17:57.800
﻿Aunt...

17:59.220 --> 18:01.770
﻿I'm going to go to the ball.

18:04.190 --> 18:05.730
﻿I'm glad...!

18:08.360 --> 18:09.570
But, isn't it strange?

18:09.980 --> 18:14.320
﻿I sometimes get the feeling that she may still be alive...

18:14.780 --> 18:16.740
﻿Somewhere underneath this sky...

18:17.530 --> 18:18.780
﻿She's still alive...

18:31.170 --> 18:33.210
﻿There is a telegram from the detectives.

18:33.880 --> 18:34.800
﻿What does it say?

18:41.140 --> 18:44.020
﻿They are searching for Lady Nadja in Milan.

18:44.410 --> 18:45.120
Milan...

18:46.140 --> 18:48.690
﻿So, she's in Italy with us...?

18:56.990 --> 18:58.780
﻿We'll leave the baby somewhere safe..

18:59.030 --> 19:01.280
﻿And, we'll tell Lady Colette that the baby died.

19:01.740 --> 19:05.000
﻿Then, I'm sure Lady Colette will agree to return to Vienna...

19:05.000 --> 19:05.750
﻿But...

19:05.960 --> 19:08.460
﻿Can't we somehow take the baby to Vienna as well?

19:08.460 --> 19:11.460
﻿No, Duke Preminger won't allow that...

19:11.960 --> 19:12.750
﻿Listen, Edna...

19:13.260 --> 19:15.710
﻿What is the best thing for Lady Colette?

19:16.010 --> 19:17.260
﻿You have to think of that!

19:18.720 --> 19:19.430
﻿And...

19:19.800 --> 19:23.850
﻿Someday, there may come a day when Lady Colette and the child will be able to meet.

19:26.350 --> 19:27.520
﻿What is it?

19:28.770 --> 19:29.690
﻿Uh... uh... um...

19:30.150 --> 19:35.610
﻿You haven't yet told Lady Colette that Lady Nadja is alive?

19:36.400 --> 19:39.530
﻿Even if I told her that she's still alive, what if they're not able to meet?

19:39.990 --> 19:43.200
It ﻿will just end up disappointing Colette.

19:43.910 --> 19:44.950
﻿And..

19:45.950 --> 19:49.580
﻿I'm not prepared to recognize Nadja as my granddaughter yet.

19:49.920 --> 19:51.630
﻿Even if the detectives bring her to me...

19:51.750 --> 19:57.130
﻿If she is not suitable for the Ducal House of Preminger then that is as far it goes.

20:00.050 --> 20:02.340
﻿Cheers!!!

20:05.270 --> 20:07.680
﻿Happy birthday, Granny.

20:07.810 --> 20:09.140
﻿Thank you.

20:09.350 --> 20:10.770
﻿Granny, here's a present!

20:10.920 --> 20:11.500
Me, too.

20:11.270 --> 20:12.100
﻿Go ahead.

20:11.500 --> 20:12.150
Here!

20:12.150 --> 20:14.270
﻿Ahh! Thank you, everybody.

20:14.730 --> 20:17.230
﻿George's present is a special poultice.

20:17.240 --> 20:19.490
﻿Thomas's is materials for hats.

20:19.530 --> 20:22.450
﻿Abel's is a cloth to polish my crystal ball.

20:22.450 --> 20:25.450
﻿Sylvie's is a handmade stomacher.

20:25.580 --> 20:27.240
﻿Wow! That's amazing!

20:27.250 --> 20:28.580
﻿You can tell without looking?

20:29.370 --> 20:31.540
﻿It's the same every year.

20:31.830 --> 20:32.670
﻿Oh.

20:33.340 --> 20:36.460
﻿But, they're all things I wanted.

20:37.170 --> 20:38.880
﻿Thank you, everyone.

20:45.760 --> 20:49.180
﻿Ohhh! This is drawn so nicely. I'm very happy.

20:49.180 --> 20:50.680
﻿Thank you, Rita.

20:52.400 --> 20:56.020
﻿Oh? So, Cream and Chocolat helped out, too!

20:56.020 --> 20:57.440
﻿Thank you.

20:58.570 --> 21:00.280
﻿Granny, from me...

21:00.280 --> 21:01.280
﻿And, me!

21:01.740 --> 21:04.660
﻿Ta-dah!

21:04.910 --> 21:06.330
﻿Roses tor Granny?

21:06.330 --> 21:07.950
﻿Well, I think they suit her well.

21:08.540 --> 21:09.790
Uh... um...

21:09.910 --> 21:14.120
I ﻿hoped you would remember something nice from the past...

21:16.750 --> 21:18.880
﻿Thank you, you two.

21:19.130 --> 21:21.340
﻿Yeah! We did it!

21:22.760 --> 21:24.260
﻿That reminds me...

21:24.640 --> 21:27.640
﻿When's your birthday, Nadja?

21:27.810 --> 21:30.140
﻿Huh? My birthday?

21:30.310 --> 21:31.930
﻿That's right! When is it?

21:32.480 --> 21:35.020
﻿I don't know my real birthday.

21:37.730 --> 21:40.980
﻿But, there were many children like that at Applefield...

21:41.320 --> 21:44.150
﻿So, the director chose our birthdays for us.

21:44.780 --> 21:46.740
﻿Mine is March 25th.

21:47.240 --> 21:49.540
﻿It's the day of the Annunciation of the Virgin Mary.

21:49.990 --> 21:54.620
﻿In that case, next year we'll have a grand celebration.

21:54.830 --> 21:57.580
﻿All right! We'll have a big party!

21:55.310 --> 21:56.730
I agree!

22:02.420 --> 22:07.640
﻿Someday, I'd like to celebrate my mother's birthday with her...

22:15.370 --> 22:18.620
Paris is sunnier than London

22:15.370 --> 22:18.620
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:18.740 --> 22:21.830
Carmen likes paella more than pasta

22:18.740 --> 22:21.830
CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:22.250 --> 22:28.420
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:22.250 --> 22:28.420
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:29.380 --> 22:30.620
Indeed

22:29.380 --> 22:30.620
Kitto

22:33.380 --> 22:35.800
It's not use worrying about it

22:33.380 --> 22:35.800
Nayan datte MUDA yo

22:36.380 --> 22:39.510
Que sera sera, sera Sera

22:36.380 --> 22:39.510
KE SERA SERA SERA SERA

22:39.770 --> 22:44.480
Tomorrow's going to be whatever it was meant

22:39.770 --> 22:44.480
Ashita nante itsumo naru you ni

22:44.560 --> 22:45.940
To be, to be

22:44.560 --> 22:45.940
Naru naru

22:46.270 --> 22:51.280
The tree fog won

22:46.270 --> 22:51.280
Sekai KAERU tobi KONKUURU

22:51.740 --> 22:55.660
The world frog-jumping contest

22:51.740 --> 22:55.660
